; =====================================================================
;  amadhi.com — DNS zone file (RFC 1035 / BIND format)
;
;  Points the website at the Hostinger VPS (srv1984615) while leaving
;  Hostinger email exactly as it is.
;
;  Authoritative nameservers per the .com registry:
;    ns1.dns-parking.com / ns2.dns-parking.com  (Hostinger DNS)
;
;  NOTE: ns1/ns2.vercel-dns.com still serve a stale copy of this zone but
;  are no longer delegated, so anything they answer is ignored by the
;  internet. Do not use them as a reference.
;
;  Generated 2026-09-30 from the live zone. Only the A and AAAA records
;  changed; mail records are reproduced verbatim.
; =====================================================================

$ORIGIN amadhi.com.
$TTL 3600

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Start of authority
;  Serial is date-based (YYYYMMDDnn); bump it on every edit.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
@       3600    IN  SOA     ns1.dns-parking.com. dns.hostinger.com. (
                            2026093004 ; serial
                            10000      ; refresh
                            2400       ; retry
                            604800     ; expire
                            600 )      ; negative TTL

@       86400   IN  NS      ns1.dns-parking.com.
@       86400   IN  NS      ns2.dns-parking.com.

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Website  →  Hostinger VPS srv1984615
;
;  Both records must change together. Leaving the old AAAA in place would
;  silently send every IPv6 visitor to the previous host while IPv4 users
;  saw the new one — the kind of split that is painful to diagnose.
;
;  TTL is deliberately short (300s) for the cutover. Raise it to 3600
;  once the move is confirmed stable.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
@       300     IN  A       201.18.193.185
@       300     IN  AAAA    2a02:4780:63:3011::1

; www is an alias of the apex, so it follows automatically.
www     300     IN  CNAME   amadhi.com.

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Email — Hostinger. DO NOT CHANGE.
;  Altering any of these stops mail delivery to @amadhi.com.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
@       14400   IN  MX      5  mx1.hostinger.com.
@       14400   IN  MX      10 mx2.hostinger.com.

; SPF — which servers may send as @amadhi.com
@       3600    IN  TXT     "v=spf1 include:_spf.mail.hostinger.com ~all"

; DMARC — currently monitor-only (p=none); see note below
_dmarc  3600    IN  TXT     "v=DMARC1; p=none"

; Outlook/Thunderbird mailbox auto-configuration
autodiscover 300 IN CNAME   autodiscover.mail.hostinger.com.

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Optional — certificate authority authorisation
;
;  There is no CAA record today, which means any CA may issue for this
;  domain. Uncommenting the lines below restricts issuance to Let's
;  Encrypt (used by the VPS) and Hostinger's CA (used for mail).
;
;  Only add this once you are sure no other service needs to issue a
;  certificate for amadhi.com — a wrong CAA record causes renewals to
;  fail silently, weeks later.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; @     3600    IN  CAA     0 issue "letsencrypt.org"
; @     3600    IN  CAA     0 issue "sectigo.com"
; @     3600    IN  CAA     0 iodef "mailto:hello@amadhi.com"

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Deliberately absent
;
;  * (wildcard)  — the live zone has none. Don't add one: it makes every
;                  typo resolve, which helps nobody and invites abuse.
;  DKIM          — not configured. Worth adding from Hostinger's mail
;                  panel; with SPF alone, DMARC can never move past
;                  p=none safely.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
